    homer_phase_actions = '<section id="homer-phase-actions" style="border-left:5px solid #c78417;background:#c7841712;padding:1.2rem;margin:1.5rem 0;line-height:1.6;overflow-wrap:anywhere"><h2>HOMER: select genomic phases and review report failures</h2>\n<p><strong>Known-only and de novo-only genomic workflows are available:</strong> <code>homer-tools genome --analysis both|known|denovo</code>, candidate <code>homer-genome-phase-candidate-2</code>, SHA starts <code>2a22d170</code>. Read <code>homer-genome-phase-validation.json</code>, <code>HOMER_GENOMIC_WORKFLOWS.md</code> and five recipes in <code>examples/homer-genome-workflow/README.md</code>. Default both retains known enrichment, discovery, matching and original reports. These supplied-FASTA/supplied-background workflows use original 5.1, 4.11 or 4.11.1 and the old-background algorithm.</p>\n<p><strong>Unrequested is not a negative finding.</strong> Successful analyses record <code>not-requested</code> status, null motif counts and no result tables for an unrequested phase. Known-only keeps chosen normalization, requires <code>known-motifs</code> and omits discovery seed/neighborhood/trial constraints. Remove <code>comparison-motifs</code>, <code>motif-length</code>, <code>mismatches</code> and <code>motifs-to-find</code>. De novo-only requires <code>comparison-motifs</code>, retains known-model matching/SVG, and omits enrichment. Remove <code>known-motifs</code> and <code>known-strand-policy</code>. Unused phase-specific options fail validation. Forward de novo-only works on all three versions without a known-enrichment strand permission; similarity to a model is not enrichment.</p>\n<p><strong>Legacy known-report division by zero: analysis FAILED, exit 2, even when the original wrapper exits 0.</strong> Original 4.11/4.11.1 infer displayed populations from rounded motif-hit percentages and can divide by zero at zero percent in <code>findKnownMotifs.pl</code>. The main warning promotes that cause and quarantines partial results. Required action: retain the failure, inspect original stderr and the complete input/model contrast, then explicitly select any scientifically appropriate separately admitted version or operation before rerunning to NEW paths. No automatic version substitution or scientific source patch. Version 5.1 guards division but can print a fallback population size of one; native audits retain actual group populations separately. A missing report is not zero enrichment.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing, forbidden, unsupported or changed dependencies: SKIP the affected analysis, exit 3.</strong> Required action: use Linux x86_64 Java 17+, inside WSL on Windows, and an admitted genomic home for the exact selected version. Where permitted run <code>install_homer_genome.py</code> with <code>--allow-install</code>, compiler/make and verified offline archives, or add <code>--allow-download</code> where permitted. If installation is forbidden or dependencies remain unavailable, retain the skip and continue independent analyses. Core/annotation homes do not admit genomic motifs. Analysis never installs or substitutes versions. All other failures exit 2: inspect warnings, session, analysis status, original diagnostics and <code>partial/</code>, correct the named cause and use a NEW output directory. Publication failures retain diagnostics at the named staging path. Partial tables are not completed results.</p>\n<p><strong>Reference and statistics still require review:</strong> preserve exact contigs, source identities, coordinates, overlap/quality/composition exclusions and all weights. BED6 is zero-based half-open; HOMER is one-based inclusive; numeric size N yields N+1. Legacy known forward selection still requires explicit original-wrapper policy or skips under require-match when enrichment is requested. Profile weights and metadata remain original. Original q uses a forward cumulative maximum, not standard BH; known log P has two print stages. Native initial weights feed an original normalization replay; learned-model bounds do not reconstruct optimization. Read the requested-phase tables and original reports. Periodic resource monitors are not OS quotas; source HTTP content pins are not independently authenticated signatures.</p>\n<p><strong>Validation and remaining work:</strong> 818 tests in 59 suites and 818 exact packaged tests per Java21/25 pass without skips. Twenty-eight complete phase protocols match 28 fresh direct original references: nine both, ten known-only and nine de novo-only. Two additional legacy zero-percentage reporting failures are rejected with promoted causes and confirmed by two fresh failing originals. Fifteen public recipe operations match fifteen further fresh originals. Four Windows host skips pass; thirteen earlier prelaunch controls remain bound by identical prelaunch production classes. Earlier 5,496 primitive comparisons and full-profile motif-family evidence retain their exact historical scopes. Historical genomic, annotation, discovery, core and native panels remain below. Generated backgrounds, named genome/repeat/TE resources, peak/coverage, RNA and GO workflows remain unfinished. HOMER keeps its missing tool-level badge; the catalog retains 250 papers, 379 tools, 2,428 observations, 682 reviewed roles and 202 supporting pointers, with 267 missing integrations. The goal and paper-wide semantic review stay active. Cell Ranger remains excluded.</p></section>'
