    homer_genome_actions = '<section id="homer-genome-actions" style="border-left:5px solid #c78417;background:#c7841712;padding:1.2rem;margin:1.5rem 0;line-height:1.6;overflow-wrap:anywhere"><h2>HOMER: supplied-background genomic motifs and required actions</h2>\n<p><strong>Original genomic workflow is available:</strong> <code>homer-tools genome</code>, development candidate <code>homer-genome-candidate-12</code>, SHA starts <code>280edbda</code>. Read <code>HOMER_GENOMIC_WORKFLOWS.md</code>, <code>homer-genome-validation.json</code> and three runnable recipes in <code>examples/homer-genome-workflow/README.md</code>. All three original releases run complete known enrichment, de novo discovery, known-motif matching and SVG/HTML reports with supplied custom FASTA and supplied background using the old algorithm. Native Java audits exact intake, coordinates, extracted sequences, composition exclusions/weights, final populations and fixed-model statistics.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing, forbidden, unsupported or changed dependencies: SKIP the affected analysis, exit 3.</strong> Required action: use Linux x86_64 Java 17+, inside WSL on Windows, and a separate admitted genomic profile for 5.1, 4.11 or 4.11.1. Where permitted run <code>python3 tools/literature/install_homer_genome.py --profile linux-x86_64-genome-5.1 --home NEW_PRIVATE_HOME --cache ARCHIVE_CACHE --report NEW_REPORT --allow-install --compiler /PATH/TO/g++ --make /PATH/TO/make --archive-dir VERIFIED_OFFLINE_ARCHIVES</code>. Add <code>--allow-download</code> only where permitted. The original extractor build requires C++11 headers, pthread, math and static C++/GCC libraries. If installation is forbidden or dependencies remain unavailable, retain the skip and continue independent analyses. Core and annotation homes do not admit genomic motifs. Analysis never installs, downloads genomes or substitutes a version. Official HTTP content pins are not independently authenticated signatures.</p>\n<p><strong>Failures exit 2 and quarantine provisional files.</strong> Required action: inspect <code>WARNINGS.md</code>, <code>analysis-status.json</code>, <code>session.json</code>, original stderr and retained <code>partial/</code> artifacts. Correct the named input, reference, parameter, resource or audit cause and rerun to a NEW output directory. Partial tables are not completed results. Preserve old homes and reports; do not edit markers to bypass changes. Readable <code>/proc</code> is required for RSS monitoring. Periodic resource monitors are not OS quotas; review heap and declared capacities.</p>\n<p><strong>Reference and population choices:</strong> BED6 is zero-based half-open; HOMER6/7 is one-based inclusive. Choose build, format, duplicate retention, unknown strand, alphabet, lowercase masking, overlap removal, GC/CpG/none weighting, strands and test explicitly. Numeric size N yields N+1 inclusive bases. Overlap removal uses separate original integer-midpoint windows before asymmetric displacement. Every source region remains in the population ledgers, including quality, unsupported-bin and overlap exclusions. Plain/gzip FASTA retains case, headers and exact contigs; Unicode paths use a UTF-8 host locale. No record is silently dropped.</p>\n<p><strong>Review original strand, matrix and statistics behavior:</strong> 4.11/4.11.1 do not forward forward-only selection to known enrichment. Default <code>known-strand-policy require-match</code> skips that configuration; explicit <code>original-wrapper</code> records BOTH known versus FORWARD normalization/discovery. Version 5.1 forwards the choice. Profile models retain raw weights and metadata; they are not calibrated probabilities. Known log P has two rounding stages. Original q uses a forward cumulative maximum, not standard BH. Original normalization replay uses independently prepared native initial weights and retained sequence order; learned-model conservative presence bounds do not reconstruct optimization. No E value or biological calibration is inferred.</p>\n<p><strong>Validation and remaining work:</strong> 805 tests in 59 suites and 805 exact packaged tests per Java21/25 pass without skips. Thirteen complete genomic protocols include nine fresh direct original comparisons, three entire known/comparison profile families (1,049/1,004/1,006 known models) and a Unicode/gzip workflow. Nine unchanged public recipes and nine further fresh original comparisons pass. Twelve prelaunch controls cover eight input failures and four capability/dependency skips; two Windows host skips pass. Native primitives match 5,496 original comparisons, including decimal ties; all nine canonical runtime bindings verify read-only. Historical annotation, discovery and fixed-core evidence remains below. Generated backgrounds, named genome/repeat/TE resources, peak/coverage, RNA and GO workflows remain unfinished. The catalog retains 250 papers, 379 tools, 2,428 observations, 682 reviewed roles and 202 supporting pointers; 38 upstream badges, 12 native-only and 267 missing integrations. HOMER keeps its missing tool-level badge. Whole-paper semantic review and the goal remain active. Cell Ranger remains excluded.</p></section>'
