    homer_annotation_actions = '<section id="homer-annotation-actions" style="border-left:5px solid #c78417;background:#c7841712;padding:1.2rem;margin:1.5rem 0;line-height:1.6;overflow-wrap:anywhere"><h2>HOMER: supplied-GTF annotation and required actions</h2>\n<p><strong>Original supplied-GTF annotation is available:</strong> <code>homer-tools annotate</code>, candidate <code>homer-annotation-candidate-3</code> (SHA starts <code>6a437815</code>). Read <code>HOMER_ANNOTATION_WORKFLOWS.md</code>, <code>homer-annotation-validation.json</code> and four recipes in <code>examples/homer-annotation/README.md</code>. Original 5.1, 4.11 or 4.11.1 runs with <code>genome none</code>, <code>size given</code> and supplied GTF. Native Java checks all peak identities, coordinates, complete populations and exact-contig nearest TSS candidates. Feature priorities, gene symbols and diagnostic enrichment statistics remain original-engine results.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing, forbidden, unsupported or pre-run changed dependencies: SKIP the affected analysis, exit 3.</strong> Required action: use Linux x86_64 Java, inside WSL on Windows, and a separate admitted annotation profile. Where allowed run <code>python3 tools/literature/install_homer_annotation.py --profile linux-x86_64-annotation-5.1 --home NEW_PRIVATE_HOME --cache ARCHIVE_CACHE --report NEW_REPORT --allow-install</code>. Choose 4.11 or 4.11.1 explicitly; add <code>--allow-download</code> only where permitted, or provide <code>--archive-dir</code> for verified offline archives. Core-only homes do not admit Perl annotation. No compiler or genome download is needed for this prebuilt subset. Analysis never installs or substitutes versions; original scientific bodies/binary bytes stay pinned, with only two script installation-path prefixes relocated. Official HTTP hashes are not independently authenticated signatures.</p>\n<p><strong>Failures exit 2 and quarantine provisional files.</strong> Read <code>WARNINGS.md</code>, <code>analysis-status.json</code>, <code>session.json</code>, <code>original.stderr</code> and retained <code>partial/</code> files. Required action: correct the named input, reference, parameter, resource or audit cause and rerun to a NEW output directory. Partial tables are not completed results. A change detected during execution invalidates provisional results. If an error precedes staging, there may be no provisional files to quarantine. Existing outputs stay intact.</p>\n<p><strong>Reference and population choices:</strong> supply exact contig lengths and declared build/annotation release; declarations do not prove compatibility. BED6 uses zero-based half-open coordinates; HOMER6/7 uses one-based inclusive coordinates. No extra columns or peaks are silently dropped. Choose duplicate-ID, dot-strand, tied-TSS and missing-GTF-contig policies explicitly. Dot becomes plus only with permission. Missing GTF contigs retain original NA, not inferred Intergenic labels. Tied nearest assignments retain every compatible native candidate; proximity does not uniquely identify a causal gene. The midpoint is <code>floor((start1+end1)/2)</code>; distance follows transcript orientation, independently of peak strand.</p>\n<p><strong>GTF sorting and metadata versions:</strong> all three originals sort selected exon rows before grouping transcripts. Raw input order and source-block counts remain retained; out-of-order rows do not create extra transcripts. Original metadata trims terminal dot-numeric versions, while Nearest PromoterID keeps the full transcript. Full GTF IDs and derived metadata IDs stay separate in <code>gtf-transcripts.tsv</code>. Ambiguous trimmed transcript-to-gene mappings fail before execution. The source Entrez ID column can contain a version-trimmed GTF gene_id. Required action: inspect actual namespaces and <code>native-tss-candidates.tsv</code>; do not silently strip source versions or treat original feature priorities/symbol conversion as native reconstruction.</p>\n<p><strong>Statistics and resources require review:</strong> <code>annotation-stats omit</code> omits the file; original diagnostics can still appear in stderr. <code>original-gtf-extent</code> preserves original statistics whose annotation/extent background is not a certified complete-genome universe. The original does not read the supplied length dictionary for that background. No q/E value or multiple-testing family is inferred. Required action: review original diagnostic denominators and source resources before inference. Readable <code>/proc</code> is required for RSS monitoring; periodic time/workspace/summed-RSS monitors are not OS quotas and shared pages can be counted more than once. Review <code>-Xmx</code> and explicit capacities.</p>\n<p><strong>Validation and remaining work:</strong> 749 tests in 54 suites and 749 exact packaged tests per Windows Java21/25 pass with no skips. All 27 annotation protocols match 27 fresh original comparisons over 120 peak rows. All 12 annotation, 12 fixed and 12 discovery public recipe operations pass. Fourteen real annotation controls retain nine input failures and five dependency/capability skips; three annotation admissions reuse without install/download. Current fixed/discovery regression retains 71/30 protocols and 45/30 fresh original comparisons. Four shared process controls, three core reuses, two Windows annotation host skips and twelve policy tests per host per installer pass. The 555 scanner comparisons/8,556 hits and earlier capacity correction remain valid. Broader named-genome/repeat/CpG resources, genomic motif wrappers, peak calling, coverage, RNA and GO workflows remain unfinished. The catalog keeps 250 papers, 379 tools, 2,428 observations, 682 reviewed uses and 202 supporting pointers; 38 upstream badges, 12 native-only and 267 missing integrations. HOMER keeps its missing tool-level badge; whole-paper semantic review and the goal remain active. Cell Ranger remains excluded.</p></section>'
    homer_annotation_actions = '<details class="homer-annotation-history"><summary>Historical supplied-GTF annotation checkpoint; current genomic workflow is above</summary>' + homer_annotation_actions + '</details>'
    homer_discovery_actions = '<section id="homer-discovery-actions" style="border-left:5px solid #c78417;background:#c7841712;padding:1.2rem;margin:1.5rem 0;line-height:1.6;overflow-wrap:anywhere"><h2>HOMER: discovery, corrections and required actions</h2>\n<p><strong>Original discovery is available:</strong> <code>homer-tools check|known|find|denovo</code>, development candidate <code>homer-discovery-candidate-2</code> (SHA starts <code>d7d187c1</code>). Read <code>HOMER_DISCOVERY_WORKFLOWS.md</code>, <code>homer-discovery-validation.json</code> and the four recipes in <code>examples/homer-discovery-workflow/README.md</code>. Native Java audits retain identities, complete populations, original model bytes, seed ledgers and final statistics. Genome/Perl annotation, peak, coverage and RNA workflows remain unfinished. HOMER retains its missing tool-level badge.</p>\n<p><strong>Correction: the earlier dense-site capacity claim was incorrect.</strong> All three original sources double the longest-sequence value before allocating site arrays. All 555 original scanner comparisons and 8,556 hits now pass, with zero exclusions. The three earlier product dense skips are invalidated. Required action: use the current candidate; <code>homer-core-candidate-1</code> retains the incorrect refusal. Original sources need no patch or compiler installation. Historical observations remain retained with the correction in <code>homer-capacity-correction.json</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing, forbidden, unsupported or changed dependencies: SKIP the affected analysis, exit 3.</strong> Required action: use Linux x86_64 Java, inside WSL on Windows, with the explicitly selected 5.1, 4.11 or 4.11.1 admitted profile. Where permitted run <code>python3 tools/literature/install_homer.py --profile linux-x86_64-5.1 --home NEW_PRIVATE_HOME --cache ARCHIVE_CACHE --report NEW_REPORT --allow-install</code>. Add <code>--allow-download</code> only where permitted, or supply <code>--archive-dir</code> for verified offline archives. Resident-memory monitoring requires readable <code>/proc</code>. Analysis never installs, switches versions or silently falls back. Preserve changed homes and failed reports. Official HTTP content hashes are not independently authenticated signatures.</p>\n<p><strong>Failures exit 2 and quarantine provisional files under partial/.</strong> Read <code>WARNINGS.md</code>, <code>analysis-status.json</code>, <code>session.json</code>, <code>original.stderr</code> and the retained ledgers. Required action: correct the named input, identity, population, parameter, resource or audit cause and rerun to a NEW output directory. Partial tables are not completed results. Existing files stay intact. Time, workspace and RSS monitoring are periodic bounds, not OS-enforced quotas.</p>\n<p><strong>Choose discovery and review its populations:</strong> select <code>full-mask</code>, <code>quick-mask-fixed</code> or <code>quick-mask-optimize</code>, explicit strands, supplied background, duplicate/overlap policies, motif length, statistic and <code>none</code> or oligo normalization. Trials must be divisible by threads. Short/N-only sequences can be seed-ineligible but remain in the complete final population. Weighted seed counts differ from final unweighted sequence-presence counts. A positive seed <code>1.000</code> is an unscored sentinel, not log P. The normalization file is an iteration snapshot, not final per-oligo weights. Original coarse P is not exact P/q/E; no multiple-testing family is inferred.</p>\n<p><strong>Printed-model uncertainty requires review:</strong> original scoring precedes repeated normalization and rounding. Keep original counts/log P beside native statistic checks, definite/possible presence bounds and a separate printed-model point rescan. Conservative envelopes of &plusmn;0.0081 per cell and &plusmn;0.000000501 for thresholds do not reconstruct the internal joint matrix. Of 36 learned models, 33 retain conservative presence uncertainty; zero point-rescan count differences occurred in these fixtures. Unresolved bounds are not exact reconstruction. Reloading a printed model is a new fixed-model analysis.</p>\n<p><strong>Validation and remaining work:</strong> 707 tests in 50 suites and 707 exact packaged tests on each Windows Java21/25 pass with no skips. Thirty discovery protocols match 30 fresh direct original comparisons; 71 fixed protocols include 58 successes, seven expected skips and three retained input failures, with 45 fresh direct original byte comparisons. All 12 discovery and 12 fixed public recipe operations pass. Four actual process controls, three admission reuses, two Windows host skips and twelve setup policy tests per host pass. The catalog keeps 250 papers, 379 tools, 2,428 observations, 682 reviewed uses and 202 supporting pointers; 38 upstream badges, 12 native-only and 267 missing integrations. Broader HOMER and paper-wide semantic review remain active. Synthetic validation does not establish biological calibration or whole-paper/production parity. Cell Ranger remains excluded.</p></section>'
